{
  "about": "Production per map building type and faction (2026-11-28). Map production types are tier slots: hq, then t1–t3, a tier split into branches with a letter (t2a, t2b); no doctrine buildings. Hand-edited: `types` (slot → the faction's CoH3 production building), `tier2` (the faction's Tier 2 building: non-tank support vehicles such as trucks, ambulances and medical half-tracks are built there), `place` (squad → building) and `research` (squad → true / false) overrides. `buildings` is written by `node tools/coh3/production.js` from CoH3 spawner data (as coh3stats' explorer lists it): `squads` are produced from the start. The HQ produces only engineers (CoH3 combat_engineer) and recon units; every other unit — doctrine (battlegroup) units and restored v214 units included — is made in the most similar tier building; only high-tier ones (heroes, heavy armour, pricier variants of a squad already produced, targets of research-locked conversions) go to `research`, researched in that building. Only squads present in the unit data are offered.",
